# A .npy program can use a unit that declares an `array of const` parameter.
# ParsePyProgram pulls builtinheap but never resolved TVarRec from it, so
# TVarRecId stayed REC_NONE and any such unit was rejected with "array of const
# requires the builtinheap unit" - while builtinheap was in fact loaded. A .npy
# program has no uses clause, so it could not work around it.
# fmtprobe is a PASCAL unit, and a bare NilPy import resolves to Python only
# (decide-nilpy-imports-that-collide-with-a-pascal-rtl-unit, user 2026-08-19),
# so the quoted spelling with the extension is how a .npy names one.
import 'fmtprobe.pas' as fmtprobe

print(fmtprobe.describe("x", 2))
